<title>Alogrithem for Evaluation Neutropenia.</title>
<graphic href="eee0269-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Degree of neutropenia</label>
<path target="cell-2">&gt;1000 to 1500 cells/microL</path>
<path target="cell-3">500 to 1000 cells/microL</path>
<path target="cell-4">&lt;500 cells/microL</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Mild neutropenia.</label>
<path target="cell-5"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Moderate neutropenia.</label>
<path target="cell-8"></path>
<path target="cell-6">If symptomatic or unstable</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Severe neutropenia </label>
<path target="cell-6"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>History and physical. If normal, repeat CBC in 4 weeks.</label>
<path target="cell-7">Normal</path>
<path target="cell-8">Persistent neutropenia or abnormal exam</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-6">
<label>If symptomatic or unstable, consider hospitalization, especially if febrile.</label>
<path target="cell-8"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Done.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-8">
<label>History and Physical, Order Blood Smear, Coomb's test, immunoglobulins, CMV, EBV, Antigranulocyte antibodies. Consider Blood and urine culture, CXR, LP if clinically indicated.</label>
<path target="cell-9">Abnormal</path>
<path target="cell-10">Normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-9">
<label>Treat empirically any underlying infectious condition. Unexplained neutropenia persists?</label>
<path target="cell-10">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-11">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-10">
<label>Consider bone marrow aspiration and genetic testing to rule out inherited disorder</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-11">
<label>Done.</label>
</cell>
</algorithm>
</algorithms>
